  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Thionyl chloride reacts with white phosphorus to produce phosphorus trichloride. The other side products in this reaction are sulphur dioxide and&nbsp;Sulphur monochloride.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>",
